JobId          → "ETL Job Id"
TriggerName    → "Triggered by"
Parameters     → "Parameter"
        ↓
Condition
        ↓
Add row to RunDetails
```

### Important

**Don't change `Compose - Columns`, `Current Row`, `Clean Row`, or `Normalized Row` yet.** They are your existing CSV parsing layer.

The only thing we're changing is **how the individual fields are selected from `Columns`**.

And this means if ADF changes from:

```text
Pipeline | Status | Run ID | Job ID
```

to:

```text
Job ID | Pipeline | Run ID | Status
```

your **Run ID will still go into RunId, Status into Status, and Job ID into JobId.**

One caution: if your CSV headers contain quoted text or unusual commas, this XPath approach depends on your existing header parsing being clean. Given your current flow, we should test **one row first (RunId + JobId)** before replacing all the other fields.
